===Verb===
{{en-verb|tapestries|tapestrying|tapestried}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|intransitive}} To [[decorate]] with tapestry, or as if with a tapestry.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1833|author=Adolphus Slade|title=Records of Travels in Turkey, Greece, &c.|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=D_EEAAAAYAAJ|page=152|section="Captain Pasha's Alarm"
|passage=We had run above twenty miles when the sun set, carpeting the sea, and '''tapestrying''' the sky with a rare unison of delicate green and golden hues {{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=September 13, 1854|author=[[w:Nathaniel Hawthorne|Nathaniel Hawthorne]]|title=English Note-Books|url=http://www.ibiblio.org/eldritch/nh/pfenb01.html|section="Conway Castle"
|passage=The banqueting-hall, all open to the sky, and with thick curtains of ivy '''tapestrying''' the walls, and grass and weeds growing on the arches that overpass it, is indescribably beautiful.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1921|author=Israel Zangwill|title=The Cockpit: Romantic Drama in Three Acts|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=6BQOAAAAMAAJ|page=255
|passage=I present Bosnavina to its Duchess, I kiss the hem of her Majesty's robe and will '''tapestry''' her Palace with conquered flags.}}

